    "title": "Dillon Brooks Caught Rage-Baiting Daniel Gafford Into Flagrant Foul At The Free-Throw Line [VIDEO] - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kenny Nosay ,\n34 minutes ago\nDillon Brooks and Daniel Gafford (Photo by @KellanOlson/X) It’s official – Dillon Brooks’ old enforcing ways are back. He was a bit silent during his two-year stint with the Houston Rockets, but now with the Suns? He’s embraced his role again as an enforcer and a villain on the court.\nJust a few days ago, Brooks was on Derik Queen’s face during a skirmish. While usually not involved in any on-court fistfights, the 29-year-old loves to get under the skin of his opponents. At 6-foot-7 and 225 pounds, he has the frame and build to handle situations like this.\nIt’s not entirely surprising that Brooks is back again in the spotlight due to his on-court persona. Against the Dallas Mavericks, he baited Daniel Gafford into a flagrant foul while standing near the free-throw line. The clip has been shared on X by Kellan Olson.\nClassic Dillon Brooks right there, folks. Gafford knew about the antics, but fell for it anyway. The shove in the face of Brooks was an unnecessary rebuttal to the trash talk. Of course, the refs saw it as intentional and assessed it as a flagrant foul. The funny thing is that the Mavericks’ big man tried to explain his actions at the end of the video.\nDillon Brooks Thriving With The Suns Dillon Brooks (Image Credits: Imagn) It’s quite obvious that Dillon Brooks has found his joy in a Phoenix Suns uniform. The pressure to win now isn’t there, but the element of surprise should they make the 2026 playoffs is an intriguing development for this team.\nAs for Brooks, this is just another day at the office for him. Getting a technical, even if he’s not in the game ? That’s pretty standard for the controversial defensive specialist. With the Suns slowly climbing up in the Western Conference standings, we’ll definitely see more Dillon Brooks ‘highlights’ for the rest of the 2025-26 season.\nThe post originally published on .",
